  "question": {
    "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math> is a complex number such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, then the minimum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math> is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>;</mo><mo> </mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Let, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>y</mi></math></p><p>And <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, which represents a circle having centre at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and radius as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> unit.</p><p>Now, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> gives the distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math> from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0037_7ec02562a8d0.png\" style=\"width: 330px; height: 246px;\"/></p><p>So, we need to find the minimum distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
}